# timer

A simple timer application built with HTML, CSS and JavaScript.  
The project serves as a hands-on front-end exercise, demonstrating real-time time handling in the browser.

## 📄 Overview

timer lets the user specify a duration (e.g. in seconds or minutes), then start a countdown. At the end of the countdown, the timer may trigger a notification or alert (depending on implementation). The whole application runs client-side, no external dependencies required.

## 🛠 Technologies Used

- **HTML5** – page structure and user controls.  
- **CSS3** – styling and layout.  
- **JavaScript** – logic for timing, event handling, and real-time UI updates.

## 🚀 How to Run

1. Clone the repository:

   git clone https://github.com/SWtheaven/timer.git

2. Navigate into the project folder:

cd timer

3. Open index.html in your browser — everything runs client-side, no extra setup needed.


4. Set the desired duration, click “Start” (or equivalent), and observe the countdown.

